{
 "id": "l42",
 "label": "42",
 "title": "Plural forms of verbs",
 "summary": "Plural verbs for plural doers and receivers: magsi- (magsikáin), magsipag- (magsipaglakád), pag- + -in (paglutuín) and pag- + -an (paghuhugasán)",
 "minutes": 40,
 "goals": [
  "Know that plural verbs are optional with plural subjects",
  "Make the plural of -um- verbs with magsi- in all forms and tenses",
  "Make the plural of mag- verbs with magsipag-",
  "Make the plural of passive -in verbs with pag- + -in",
  "Make the plural of passive -an verbs with pag- + -an, including irregular roots"
 ],
 "sections": [
  {
   "title": "Plural verbs: useful, not compulsory",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "p",
     "t": "You met the **plurality rule** back in Lesson 4: when the subject is plural, other words in the sentence can take plural forms too. Verbs have plural forms as well."
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "t": "The grammar book **Balarila ng Wikang Pambansa**, written by Lope K. Santos in 1939 as head of the Institute of National Language, says that using plural verbs with plural subjects is **not compulsory**. A plural subject with a singular verb **does not make the sentence wrong**."
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "t": "Native speakers can easily say long plural verbs such as **mangagsikáin**, **mangagkaín**, **magsipagkaín**, **mangágsipagkáinan** and **mangagkaínan**, but learners find them very hard to pronounce. So this lesson sticks to **four simpler plural affixes**, two for each voice:"
    },
    {
     "type": "table",
     "head": [
      "Voice",
      "Singular verb type",
      "Plural affix"
     ],
     "rows": [
      [
       "Active (focus on the doer or the act)",
       "-um- (Lesson 14)",
       "[[magsi-|pred]]"
      ],
      [
       "Active (focus on the doer or the act)",
       "mag- (Lesson 14)",
       "[[magsipag-|pred]]"
      ],
      [
       "Passive (focus on the receiver)",
       "-in (Lesson 15)",
       "[[pag- + -in|pred]] (or pag- + -hin)"
      ],
      [
       "Passive (focus on the receiver)",
       "-an (Lesson 33)",
       "[[pag- + -an|pred]] (or pag- + -han)"
      ]
     ],
     "title": "The four plural affixes in this lesson"
    },
    {
     "type": "box",
     "kind": "tip",
     "title": "Enough for real conversation",
     "t": "The book says these four affixes are enough to give a learner the plural verbs needed for an advanced Tagalog conversation."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Magsi-: plural of -um- verbs",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "p",
     "t": "**Magsi-** makes the plural of **-um- verbs**. It works like mag-: **m** changes to **n** for the past and present, and the present and future repeat **si**, the second syllable of magsi-."
    },
    {
     "type": "pattern",
     "title": "magsi- + root",
     "rows": [
      {
       "label": "Infinitive",
       "chips": [
        {
         "t": "magsi-",
         "r": "pred"
        },
        {
         "t": "kain",
         "r": "pred"
        },
        {
         "t": "→ magsikáin",
         "r": "pred"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "label": "Past",
       "chips": [
        {
         "t": "nagsi-",
         "r": "pred"
        },
        {
         "t": "kain",
         "r": "pred"
        },
        {
         "t": "→ nagsikáin",
         "r": "pred"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "label": "Present",
       "chips": [
        {
         "t": "nagsi-",
         "r": "pred"
        },
        {
         "t": "+ si",
         "r": "pred"
        },
        {
         "t": "kain",
         "r": "pred"
        },
        {
         "t": "→ nagsísikáin",
         "r": "pred"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "label": "Future",
       "chips": [
        {
         "t": "magsi-",
         "r": "pred"
        },
        {
         "t": "+ si",
         "r": "pred"
        },
        {
         "t": "kain",
         "r": "pred"
        },
        {
         "t": "→ magsísikáin",
         "r": "pred"
        }
       ]
      }
     ],
     "note": "to eat · ate · are eating · will eat"
    },
