    {
     "type": "box",
     "kind": "rule",
     "title": "O changes to u",
     "t": "The **o** in luto changes to **u** when the -in ending is added (the infinitive, imperative and future): lutò → paglut**u**ín, paglúlut**u**ín. Other verbs that end in the vowel **o** make the same change."
    },
    {
     "type": "box",
     "kind": "remember",
     "title": "Look back at Lesson 15",
     "t": "Lesson 15 explains how -in verbs behave when the root ends in a vowel, with or without a glottal catch, and when to use **-hin** instead of -in. The same applies here: pagbasa**hín**."
    },
    {
     "type": "vocab",
